      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To expand the expression \\((2x + 3)(x + 5)\\), we will use the distributive property, also known as the FOIL method (First, Outer, Inner, Last) for binomials. Here are the steps:\n\n1. **Multiply the First terms**: \\(2x \\cdot x = 2x^2\\)\n2. **Multiply the Outer terms**: \\(2x \\cdot 5 = 10x\\)\n3. **Multiply the Inner terms**: \\(3 \\cdot x = 3x\\)\n4. **Multiply the Last terms**: \\(3 \\cdot 5 = 15\\)\n\nNow, we combine all these products:\n\\[\n2x^2 + 10x + 3x + 15\n\\]\n\nNext, we combine the like terms \\(10x\\) and \\(3x\\):\n\\[\n2x^2 + 13x + 15\n\\]\n\nThus, the expanded form of \\((2x + 3)(x + 5)\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2x^2 + 13x + 15}\n\\]",
